      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>PeopleCert had been planning to cut about 400 jobs in £22m savings drive at training body it bought last year</p><p>The vocational training body City &amp; Guilds has guaranteed that plans for mass compulsory redundancies and the offshoring of hundreds of UK jobs to Greece will no longer go ahead.</p><p>The proposal to remove about 400 UK roles was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/dec/14/city-guilds-uk-workforce-peoplecert-cost-cutting-drive\">first reported by the Guardian in December</a> as part of a £22m cost-cutting drive after the acquisition of the charity’s training and awards business by the Greek-owned PeopleCert in October.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/education/2026/jun/18/city-and-guilds-scraps-mass-redundancies-offshoring-uk-jobs-to-greece\">Continue reading...</a>"
